PHASE 6 — TOPIC PAGE V2

The Course → Branch → Subject → Topic hierarchy has now been implemented on the development server.

Now improve ONLY the topic/note page experience.

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT redesign the homepage.
- Do NOT redesign /notes.
- Do NOT implement MCQs yet.
- Do NOT implement authentication.
- Do NOT implement payments.
- Do NOT implement AI chatbot.
- Do NOT add unnecessary dependencies.
- Do NOT rewrite existing Markdown content unnecessarily.
- Preserve existing public URLs.
- Reuse the existing design system/components where possible.

==================================================
GOAL
==================================================

Create one excellent, reusable exam-focused topic page template.

Use an existing topic such as:

Decision Tree

as the reference implementation.

After the template is complete, apply it to existing notes only if the existing content supports the sections.

==================================================
TOPIC PAGE STRUCTURE
==================================================

The page should follow this structure:

1. Breadcrumbs

Example:

Home
→ Notes
→ BTech
→ CSE
→ Machine Learning
→ Decision Tree

Every breadcrumb item should be a real internal link.

--------------------------------------------------

2. Topic Header

Show:

Topic title

Example:
Decision Tree in Machine Learning

Academic context:

BTech
CSE
Machine Learning
Unit 2 — Supervised Learning

Short topic description.

Do not invent academic metadata.

Only display metadata that exists in the content model.

--------------------------------------------------

3. Exam Navigation

Add a compact navigation area:

[ 2 MARKS ]
[ 5 MARKS ]
[ 10 MARKS ]
[ QUICK REVISION ]

These should anchor-link to sections on the same page.

On mobile, this should remain easy to use.

--------------------------------------------------

4. Quick Definition

Create:

## Definition

A concise exam-friendly definition.

Do not generate fake content.

If the existing Markdown contains a suitable definition, use it.

--------------------------------------------------

5. 2-Mark Answer

Create:

## 2-Mark Answer

This should be short and directly usable in an exam.

Add a "Copy Answer" button if technically simple.

The copy button should:
- copy only the answer
- show a small success state
- work on desktop and mobile
- not require authentication

--------------------------------------------------

6. 5-Mark Answer

Create:

## 5-Mark Answer

Use the existing note content where possible.

Structure with:
- definition
- key points
- working/steps
- small example where available

Keep it exam-oriented.

--------------------------------------------------

7. 10-Mark Answer

Create:

## 10-Mark Answer

This is the primary section.

Make it visually prominent.

Where appropriate include:

- Introduction
- Definition
- Working
- Algorithm/steps
- Formula
- Example
- Diagram
- Advantages
- Disadvantages
- Applications
- Conclusion

Do NOT force sections that are not relevant to the topic.

--------------------------------------------------

8. Diagrams

Where a diagram exists in the Markdown/content:

- render it correctly
- provide useful alt text
- make it responsive
- prevent overflow on mobile

Do not create fake diagrams.

If no diagram exists, do not create a placeholder.

--------------------------------------------------

9. Important Concepts

Show the important concepts already present in the note.

For example:

- Entropy
- Information Gain
- Gini Index
- Pruning

Do not invent concepts.

--------------------------------------------------

10. Example

If the note has an example, display it clearly.

Use:

## Example

Make numerical examples easy to read.

Tables should be responsive.

--------------------------------------------------

11. Advantages and Disadvantages

Where supported by the content:

## Advantages

## Disadvantages

Do not create empty headings.

--------------------------------------------------

12. Applications

Where supported:

## Applications

Again, do not invent content.

--------------------------------------------------

13. Important Exam Questions

Add:

## Important Exam Questions

Use questions that already exist in the note/content model.

Do not claim that questions are "frequently asked" unless there is actual evidence.

Use neutral wording such as:

"Important questions to prepare"

--------------------------------------------------

14. Quick Revision

Add:

## Quick Revision

Create a concise revision summary based ONLY on the actual note.

Example format:

- Definition
- Key concept
- Formula
- Main steps
- Advantages
- Limitations

Do not generate meaningless filler.

--------------------------------------------------

15. Related Topics

Add:

## Related Topics

Only link to notes that actually exist.

Use the existing relatedSlugs/metadata if available.

Do not generate broken links.

--------------------------------------------------

16. Previous / Next

At the bottom:

[← Previous Topic]    [Next Topic →]

Navigation should follow the existing academic/topic order.

Do not use alphabetical order unless that is already the intended order.

If there is no previous or next topic, hide that button.

--------------------------------------------------

17. Parent Subject CTA

At the bottom provide:

"Back to Machine Learning Notes"

or equivalent based on actual metadata.

This must link to the actual subject page.

==================================================
DESIGN REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

The topic page should feel like an EXAM PREPARATION PAGE, not a blog article.

Prioritize:

- readability
- whitespace
- clear headings
- exam-focused sections
- mobile usability
- fast loading

Use the existing visual design.

Do not introduce a completely new design language.

--------------------------------------------------

MOBILE
--------------------------------------------------

Test the topic page at mobile width.

Check:

- breadcrumbs
- title
- exam navigation
- tables
- diagrams
- long answers
- copy button
- previous/next navigation

No accidental horizontal overflow.

--------------------------------------------------

SEO
--------------------------------------------------

For each topic page verify:

- one H1
- logical H2/H3 hierarchy
- unique title
- unique meta description
- canonical URL
- Open Graph metadata where already supported
- breadcrumb structured data if appropriate

Example title:

Decision Tree in Machine Learning | 10-Mark Exam Answer

Do not blindly use this exact title for every topic.

Generate metadata from the actual topic.

--------------------------------------------------

ACCESSIBILITY
--------------------------------------------------

Check:

- button labels
- keyboard navigation
- focus states
- image alt text
- heading hierarchy
- color contrast

Do not rely only on color to communicate state.

==================================================
IMPLEMENTATION
==================================================

